"""SkillExecutor — skill lifecycle, phase advancement, tool dispatch.

The SkillExecutor is the single object responsible for:

1. **Skill lifecycle** — activating, completing, digresssing, and resuming
   skills by mutating the dialogue stack via ``TrackerHandle``.
2. **Deterministic phase advancement** — advancing through ``utter``,
   ``noop``, ``collect``, and ``update_session`` steps before the LLM is
   invoked.
3. **Tool dispatch** — routing every LLM tool call to the right handler,
   including batch ``set_fields`` memory writes.

All flows belong to skills and are resolved exclusively from the
``SkillCatalog`` — there is no separate ``FlowsList``.

Lifecycle invariant
-------------------
All tracker mutations go through ``TrackerHandle.apply_events``.  The
SkillExecutor never calls ``tracker.update`` directly.

Stack hard-cut
--------------
``_activate`` pushes only ``SkillStackFrame`` /
``OrderedBlockStackFrame`` (fail-closed otherwise). Remaining
``UserFlowStackFrame`` branches advance, park, or cancel frames that may
still appear from historical patches or in-flight sessions — they are not
a live Mantle activate path. Remove them once live flow cursors are gone.

Design note — two distinct action concepts
-------------------------------------------
**Deterministic action steps** (``ActionStep`` with ``action_*``) are decided
by the skill, not the LLM.  They are advanced in ``advance_steps`` and, when
implemented, will call the Rasa action server synchronously.

**Builder-defined LLM tools** are ``@tool``-decorated async functions defined
in ``skills/<skill_id>/tools.py``.  ``skill.md`` ``import_tools`` and
``tool_constraints`` control which tools the LLM may call; descriptions and
parameter schemas are derived from the Python function signature at model-load
time.  These tools are dispatched in-process via ``call_tool_func`` — not
through the action server.

Open TODOs
----------
* **ActionStep — custom action dispatch**: non-utter action steps in
  ``advance_steps`` currently break out of the loop (the LLM receives the
  step as context).  A full implementation must call the Rasa action server,
  await the response, apply the returned events, and then continue the loop.
* **Collect — custom ask action**: collect steps whose ``collect_action``
  is an ``action_ask_*`` (not an ``utter_ask_*``) need the same action-server
  dispatch path.
* **Collect — memory validation and rejection re-prompt**: ``step.rejections``
  is not yet evaluated.  Memory values are accepted unconditionally; invalid
  values silently succeed instead of triggering a rejection utterance and
  re-asking.
"""

